WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.392
This is JobMarket Lens,

00:00:02.392 --> 00:00:04.164
the research canvas.

00:00:04.164 --> 00:00:06.842
82,000 job postings from S&P 500

00:00:06.842 --> 00:00:09.239
career sites.

00:00:09.239 --> 00:00:10.063
Its promise:

00:00:10.063 --> 00:00:11.093
see the demand,

00:00:11.093 --> 00:00:12.475
then check the evidence.

00:00:12.475 --> 00:00:13.765
Here's how,

00:00:13.765 --> 00:00:15.001
in 90 seconds.

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:16.761
Everything starts from one question.

00:00:16.761 --> 00:00:17.987
The scope line tells

00:00:17.987 --> 00:00:19.152
you what you're looking at:

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:22.049
a snapshot of reported and observed postings,

00:00:22.049 --> 00:00:23.521
not real-time vacancies.

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:28.681
The demand landscape shows where roles meet employers.

00:00:28.681 --> 00:00:29.974
Select one cell,

00:00:29.974 --> 00:00:32.728
say computer and math at Amazon,

00:00:32.728 --> 00:00:34.776
and every panel follows.

00:00:34.776 --> 00:00:37.186
222 postings,

00:00:37.186 --> 00:00:40.095
with their pay ranges and locations.

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:41.494
To compare,

00:00:41.494 --> 00:00:43.421
pick an occupation and

00:00:43.421 --> 00:00:44.476
pin it as view A.

00:00:44.476 --> 00:00:46.071
Then pick another,

00:00:46.071 --> 00:00:46.596
sales,

00:00:46.596 --> 00:00:48.436
and pin it as view B.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.886
Both views stay frozen,

00:00:50.886 --> 00:00:51.929
side by side.

00:00:51.929 --> 00:00:55.055
7,963 postings

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:57.642
against 15,604.

00:00:57.642 --> 00:01:00.087
Every difference shows its counts.

00:01:00.087 --> 00:01:02.171
Python appears in 3,621

00:01:02.171 --> 00:01:04.015
tech postings,

00:01:04.015 --> 00:01:06.164
and 103 in sales.

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:10.507
Skill connections reads the shared language of postings.

00:01:10.507 --> 00:01:12.625
Communication and data analysis

00:01:12.625 --> 00:01:15.308
appear together in 19,242

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:16.911
of them.

00:01:16.911 --> 00:01:18.497
A mention is a clue,

00:01:18.497 --> 00:01:19.727
not a requirement.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.992
Evidence and sources shows

00:01:21.992 --> 00:01:23.663
what a selection can support:

00:01:23.663 --> 00:01:25.433
how much text was analyzed,

00:01:25.433 --> 00:01:26.506
what's unknown,

00:01:26.506 --> 00:01:28.613
and how many pay ranges are valid.

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:31.088
Every number has an origin,

00:01:31.088 --> 00:01:34.971
from the pinned upstream snapshot to local observations.

00:01:34.971 --> 00:01:37.712
And inventory is not hiring growth.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.493
Found a useful view?

00:01:40.493 --> 00:01:41.701
Share the study,

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:44.834
and anyone opens exactly the same question.

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:47.627
Start at lens.feedos.si.
